  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This started as of the recent update to fix avatars in FBT jittering when the user turned their head, where the solution was to immobilize the player when they were not moving. \n\nUpon triggering an animation, the avatar will face whatever direction you were immobilized in, usually the wrong direction. For example, if you walk somewhere, turn your head to one side, do an emote, the emote faces forwards (the direction you walked) instead of to the side (where your head is pointing). If you then turn your head during the animation, the avatar does not follow. \n\nThis gets very annoying using FBT in room-scale where I will frequently physically turn around to look at people, but when I try to use an animation (e.g. point) my avatar turns to face the wrong direction.",
